-\noindent\textbf{UV4: SpecLFB: ROB Walk Order.}\label{sec:uv4-speclfb-rob-walk} This bug widens A-UV6: AMuLeT reports SpecLFB's unprotected load only for the first speculative load~\cite[\S 4.7]{amulet}, and its patch for A-UV6 would also close this bug. SpecLFB~\cite{cheng2024speclfb} decides whether a speculative load is unsafe in two walks: the ROB walk marks a load that has no older unsafe load, and the LSQ walk flags loads in a branch's shadow. A load is held only if it is flagged and was not marked. At gem5's default delays, a load reaches the ROB one cycle before it reaches the load queue, so the ROB walk can mark a younger load before the LSQ walk has flagged the older one, and the mark is never cleared. Loads after the first speculative load can therefore go unprotected as well. In 398 of the first 4{,}000 tests, only a later load leaks.
